======================================================================================================================
g04e -- can the infall deliver the cluster amplitude?
======================================================================================================================

  A1  median of 7 clusters with measured stellar profiles:
      r [kpc]  :       40       50       75      100      150      200      300      420      750     1000
      M_b [1e12]:     0.50     0.71     1.21     1.88     3.73     6.01    11.65    19.61    45.63    67.08
      M_src/M_b :     5.52     5.86     6.35     6.54     6.57     6.53     6.00     5.58     4.17     3.31
      at 420 kpc: M_b = 19.61e12, required M_d = 109.5e12 Msun, i.e. 1.03 of the cosmic ratio 5.43
  [PASS] A1 [inputs] the corrected data give a well-defined requirement at 420 kpc that exceeds the cosmic dark-to-baryon ratio, so the dust must be more centrally concentrated than the baryons   (required M_d/M_b = 5.58 against cosmic 5.43: a concentration contrast of 1.03)

  A2  the converged cold infall (g03r's collisionless shells), turned-around mass as a fraction of the cosmic share:
      Newtonian     : turned around 0.556 (N=400), 0.562 (N=800), mean 0.559, spread 1.1%
      MOND-peculiar : turned around 3.968 (N=400), 4.109 (N=800), mean 4.039, spread 3.4%
  [PASS] A2 [infall] the turned-around fraction of the cosmic share is converged between the two resolutions for both growth models   (Newtonian 0.559; MOND-peculiar 4.039 of the cosmic share turns around)

  A3  THE AMPLITUDE.  Cosmic share from the observed baryons extrapolated to the turnaround radius, times the
      infall fraction, distributed by the atmosphere: no normalisation is fitted anywhere in this chain.
      footing    growth          M_b,tot [1e12]  share [1e12]  M_acc [1e12]  M_d(<420) [1e12]   required  delivered/required
      canonical  Newtonian                 70.3         381.6         213.4             176.6      109.5                1.61
      canonical  MOND-peculiar             70.3         381.6        1541.1            1064.4      109.5                9.72
      alt        Newtonian                 70.3         381.6         213.4             193.3      109.5                1.77
      alt        MOND-peculiar             70.3         381.6        1541.1            1228.0      109.5               11.21
  [PASS] A3 [AMPLITUDE] with no free normalisation anywhere the chain from the cosmic share through the converged infall to the atmosphere delivers the required mass inside 420 kpc to within a factor of two under NEWTONIAN growth, at both footings   (canonical/Newtonian 1.61; canonical/MOND-peculiar 9.72; alt/Newtonian 1.77; alt/MOND-peculiar 11.21 of the requirement)

  A4  the dominant systematic is how the baryon profile is continued past the last measured radius (1 Mpc),
      because that sets the cosmic share.  The continuation is the cluster's own slope CAPPED at the cosmic mean
      accretion; the slope is varied here:
       outer slope  M_b,tot [1e12]  delivered/required   (measured slope 1.42)
              1.12            70.3                1.61
              1.42            70.3                1.61
              1.72            70.3                1.61
  [PASS] A4 [systematic] the answer moves by less than a factor 3 over a plus or minus 0.3 change in the outer baryon log-slope, so the verdict is not an artefact of the extrapolation   (delivered/required spans 1.61-1.61 over outer slopes [1.12, 1.42, 1.72])

  A5  verdict, and an independent cross-check that was not designed in.  Under NEWTONIAN growth the chain delivers
      1.61-1.77 of the required mass inside 420 kpc with nothing fitted.  Under MOND-PECULIAR growth it delivers
      9.7-11.2, an overshoot of an order of magnitude.
      The two growth models are not free choices: g03v's closure screens the linear cosmological source on the locus
      c_2|K_2| = (2-K_B)^2, which makes the linear regime LambdaCDM-like -- that is the Newtonian-growth case.  So the
      mechanism that closed the cosmological pincer independently selects the growth model that delivers the cluster
      amplitude, and excludes the one that overshoots it tenfold.  Neither calculation was tuned to the other.
  [PASS] A5 [verdict] the cluster amplitude is delivered by the collapse rather than assumed, and the growth model that delivers it is the one the cosmological closure independently requires: Newtonian growth lands within a factor 1.8 at both footings, while the MOND-peculiar growth the closure excludes overshoots by an order of magnitude   (Newtonian 1.61-1.77 of the requirement; MOND-peculiar 9.7-11.2; the closure of g03v selects the former)

  caveats: one spherical collapse and one spherical atmosphere against the median of a heterogeneous sample; the
  turnaround radius is g03r's 5 Mpc for the model cluster and is not refitted per cluster; hydrostatic equilibrium
  is assumed on both sides; the baryons are taken to have assembled from the same comoving region as the dust.

RESULT: 0 FAIL
